(99, '2027-01-25', 3, 14, 'Read EZKL source — inference pipeline and lookup arguments', 'Week Review: Commit to the KudiSense private credit-scoring use case as the flagship zkML project scope — a model that proves a credit decision is correctly computed without revealing the applicant''s underlying financial data. Review this week''s DSAR structures.', 'Daily DSAR rep: Toy polynomial commitment — implement and verify a simple Pedersen or KZG-style commitment.'),
(100, '2027-01-26', 3, 15, 'Circuit security — how real ZK circuits break', 'Read 5-6 real documented circuit vulnerabilities from the 0xPARC ZK Bug Tracker and Trail of Bits'' public ZK audit findings. For each, identify: what constraint was missing, what a malicious witness could have done with it, and how it was caught. *(Resource: [0xPARC ZK Bug Tracker](https://github.com/0xPARC/zk-bug-tracker))*', 'Daily DSAR rep: Finite field arithmetic — implement modular add/mul/inverse over a prime field by hand.'),
(101, '2027-01-27', 3, 15, 'Circuit security — how real ZK circuits break', 'Deep dive on under-constrained signals specifically: study 2-3 historical Circom/Halo2 under-constraint bugs and reproduce a minimal toy circuit that has the same class of bug. *(Resource: [Trail of Bits ZK blog series](https://blog.trailofbits.com/category/zero-knowledge/))*', 'Daily DSAR rep: Finite field arithmetic — implement modular add/mul/inverse over a prime field by hand.'),
(102, '2027-01-28', 3, 15, 'Circuit security — how real ZK circuits break', 'Study soundness vs completeness as a practical checklist, not just theory: write your own one-page checklist you''ll run against your own KudiSense circuit before you trust it. *(Resource: [ZK Hack Whiteboard Sessions](https://zkhack.dev/whiteboard/))*', 'Daily DSAR rep: Finite field arithmetic — implement modular add/mul/inverse over a prime field by hand.'),
(103, '2027-01-29', 3, 15, 'Circuit security — how real ZK circuits break', 'Read an introduction to formal verification for arithmetic circuits (what tools like Picus or the Ecne prover actually check). You don''t need to run one yet — understand what class of bug they catch that manual review misses. *(Resource: [Picus README](https://github.com/Veridise/Picus))*', 'Daily DSAR rep: Finite field arithmetic — implement modular add/mul/inverse over a prime field by hand.'),
(104, '2027-02-01', 3, 15, 'Circuit security — how real ZK circuits break', 'Run your soundness/completeness checklist against the EZKL-based circuit architecture you scoped for KudiSense last week. Write down every place you''re currently trusting the framework rather than verifying it yourself.', 'Daily DSAR rep: Finite field arithmetic — implement modular add/mul/inverse over a prime field by hand.'),
(105, '2027-02-02', 3, 15, 'Circuit security — how real ZK circuits break', 'Week Review: Write a short internal doc — ''How I''d try to break my own KudiSense circuit'' — listing the 3 most plausible attack vectors and how you''ll test for each once it''s built. This doc becomes part of your project writeup later. Review this week''s DSAR structures.', 'Daily DSAR rep: Finite field arithmetic — implement modular add/mul/inverse over a prime field by hand.'),
(106, '2027-02-03', 3, 16, 'zkML flagship — KudiSense private credit-scoring circuit', 'Finalize the architecture for the KudiSense zkML flagship: a privacy-preserving credit-scoring model where an applicant''s financial data never leaves their device, but the credit decision is verifiably correct on-chain. Define the ONNX architecture accordingly, sized to the real signals KudiSense already models (spending pattern, income regularity, repayment history). *(Resource: [PyTorch ONNX Export](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/onnx.html))*', 'Daily DSAR rep: Merkle proof edge cases — non-power-of-2 leaf counts, rejecting a malicious/forged proof.'),
(107, '2027-02-04', 3, 16, 'zkML flagship — KudiSense private credit-scoring circuit', 'Train the PyTorch model locally. Keep it small enough to ensure manageable proving times (e.g., <1M parameters). *(Resource: [PyTorch Training Loop](https://pytorch.org/tutorials/beginner/blitz/cifar10_tutorial.html))*', 'Daily DSAR rep: Merkle proof edge cases — non-power-of-2 leaf counts, rejecting a malicious/forged proof.'),
(108, '2027-02-05', 3, 16, 'zkML flagship — KudiSense private credit-scoring circuit', 'Export the model to `.onnx` and perform a dry-run inference using Python''s `onnxruntime` to ensure accuracy. *(Resource: [ONNX Runtime Python](https://onnxruntime.ai/docs/get-started/with-python.html))*', 'Daily DSAR rep: Merkle proof edge cases — non-power-of-2 leaf counts, rejecting a malicious/forged proof.'),
